"**Answer:**  \nThe Associate Editor is **Matthew\u202fJ. Goff**.\n\n**Why he fits every part of the question**\n\n| Requirement | How Matthew\u202fJ.\u202fGoff satisfies it |\n|-------------|---------------------------------|\n| **Graduate of the University of Chicago** | Goff earned his Ph.D. in Biblical Studies from the University of Chicago Divinity School in 2002. |\n| **Teaches at a public university in Florida** | He is an Associate Professor of Religion at Florida State University, a public research university in Tallahassee, Florida. |\n| **Co\u2011authored a 2014 article on the Qumran manuscripts with Dennis Duke** | In 2014, Goff co\u2011authored the article \u201cThe Astronomy of the Qumran Fragments 4Q208 and 4Q209\u201d with Dennis\u202fDuke, published in *Dead Sea Discoveries* (vol.\u202f21, pp.\u202f176\u2011210). |\n| **Associate Editor of the SBL Study Bible** | Goff is listed as one of the associate editors of the *SBL Study Bible: New Revised Standard Version, Updated Edition* (SBL Publications, 2021). |\n\nThus, Matthew\u202fJ.\u202fGoff is the person you\u2019re looking for."